France and England later Britain have  not had the best relationship in the 500  years before the end of Napoleon the two  have been at war for a hundred and sixty  four of them and the rest of them they  spent not exactly being keen on one  another yet throughout the last seven  hundred years there have been numerous  attempts to unify the two entities but  how close did they come to fruition did  Britain and France almost become one  country now the first time that there  was any real chance of unification was  at the height of the Hundred Years War  when England for the help of Burgundy  had won numerous victories their success  peaked in 1422 when the child King Henry  the sixth was crowned King Henry ii of  france now henry didn't control all of  france and with the help of a certain  Joan of Arc France won the Hundred Years  War and the English were pushed out King  George the 3rd was the last British mana  to formally claim the French throne  since he renounced his claim in 1801  when Great Britain was merged with  Island so it was in 1940 that the most  famous attempt to unify the two came  about this happened after the Allied  front line collapsed and France was on  the brink of being conquered by Germany  naturally everyone was panicking and so  the British made a proposal both nations  and their empire should unify into a  single entity the franco-british Union  the new constitution was going to be  drafted which would unite some of the  organs of government defense and foreign  policy would be conducted from London  the nation's new capital whereas the new  nation's finances would be administered  from French territory what was left of  it that is the British and French  Parliament's would as a stopgap have to  both pass the same legislation for it to  come into effect until they were merged  the positions of each of the head of  state would be extended to the other  meaning France would have a king again  and Britain would have a president  beyond this there weren't many concrete  plans because everyone was panicking  about the war in France surrendering  also as a side note it was expected that  the other states that have fallen to  Germany would also join this Union too  so it wouldn't be France and Britain for  long in the end these proposals never  went anywhere because whilst prominent  politicians on both sides favoured the  Union many Frenchmen didn't want to sign  their country's existence away many of  them felt that they were being forced to  choose between military submission to  Germany or political and economic  submission to Britain and they chose the  former the next and final time many  politicians attempted to merge the two  nations was in 1956 after the Suez  Crisis which saw Britain France and  Israel invade Egypt to prevent it from  seizing the Suez Canal was an absolute  failure the two powers became desperate  it was an international embarrassment  and it looked clear to both that they  were now firmly junior partners to the  USA if they were to protect their  crumbling empires something would need  to be done as such guy Malay the French  Prime Minister proposed the  franco-british union to the British  Prime Minister Harold Macmillan the plan  was that both would unite into a single  nation with Queen Elizabeth the second  taking the title queen of France this  government would be devolved and both  would maintain separate budgets but  their armed forces and empires would be  merged and it was hoped that the two  combined would act as a third pillar in  the Cold War  this time discussions didn't go very far  McMillan said no and the reason was that  there was literally a 0% chance that the  British or French publics would have  gone along with this McMillan was  personally against the Union and  preferred for a new European economic  Union to counterbalance the USSR in the  USA which did happen and to which  Britain wasn't invited after this both  nations would remain separate in the  franco-british Union would go down as a  curious idea brought up when both  nations faced a crisis I hope you  enjoyed this episode and thank you for  watching with the special thanks to my  patrons James Bissonnette John lucid a  man of culture Danny Maloney little  holiday John biscuits Rob Waterhouse mo  James Castaneda Aaron the White Jordan  Longley Gustav Swan marcus asana rashid  ali spinning three plates filled oink  oink David Silverman  Maggie packs Kowski Spencer Lightfoot  Lexi Schwinn Kelly moneymaker  Anthony Beckett Robert Wetzel Skye  Chappell Marvin Castle Winston Hayward  and Izzy also let's be reasonable it  would have fallen apart like five  minutes after the war was over
 

